cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  leo-wsn: an ns-3 reconstruction of the LEO routing metric with
  mobility and parameter-sensitivity analysis
message: >-
  If you use this software or the datasets it produces, please cite both
  this software entry and the accompanying paper, and cite the original
  LEO metric publication (listed under references) for the metric itself.
type: software
authors:
  # REPLACE with the real author list before publishing. Order and
  # affiliations should match the paper.
  - given-names: FIRST
    family-names: LAST
    affiliation: INSTITUTION
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/USER/REPO'
abstract: >-
  An independent ns-3 reconstruction of the Low Energy and Overhead (LEO)
  wireless-sensor-network routing metric, together with hop-count and two
  ZigBee LQI baselines, an equation-level verification oracle, route
  discrimination screening, statistical significance testing, and a
  static-versus-mobile evaluation across six topology layouts. The
  repository documents every modeling assumption and every deviation from
  the source publication, including two findings that materially affect
  interpretation: the published nRF52840 LQI cost formulation degenerates
  to hop-count at realistic node spacing, and the sign of the LEO energy
  comparison inverts across the range of a per-flood re-relay bound that
  the source publication does not specify.
keywords:
  - wireless sensor networks
  - routing metrics
  - ns-3
  - energy-efficient routing
  - reproducibility
  - simulation validation
  - node mobility
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-01-01'

